  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Volunteers (UNV) programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Arrangement for joint activities that support international development through United Nations (UN) volunteer assignments. Australian volunteers will complete assignments focussed on UN reform and human rights (including disability inclusion, gender equality and women&#x2019;s empowerment) in developing countries in the Pacific, with a limited number completing assignments in Headquarters. This investment will promote greater awareness of the value of volunteer action for development. The total value of this investment is $1.5 million to be expensed over two years, starting in the 2018-19 financial year.</narrative>
  </description>
